;; Same form as spelling-fqdn.wat and spelling-clojure.wat. ≥2 defn args, ≥2 let binders.
;; .wat.bad: the checker does not treat :wat.core/defn as defn (Doctrine 1 on the
;; type keywords). The formatter still rules it. The clojure target --checks.
(:wat.core/defn :fix::two
  [a <- :wat::core::i64
   b <- :wat::core::i64]
  -> :wat::core::i64
  (:wat.core/let
    [x a
     y b]
    x))
